@@ -1,5 +1,14 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.2 (unreleased)
+
+Additive only; no breaking change. Not compiled or run.
+
+- Orthic-Labs/rightkit#449: `playback` gains thread-owned app playback. `OutputSession::start(source, PlaybackOptions)` returns a Send-safe `OutputPlayback` (cpal stream and decoder stay on one owner thread) fed from a `PlaybackSource` (random-access decoded PCM). Linear-interpolating rate/speed conversion and channel mapping, `seek_samples`, `set_speed` (1/16..=16), `stop`/`resume`, `flush`, `cursor_samples`, `set_gain`, `take_last_error`. New `OutputGain`, a cloneable shared 0..=4 gain handle that survives reopens and is applied before the callback is created (silent QA from the first sample). Ported from patch G3.
+- New feature `test-mode` (implies `playback`, QA builds only): `FakeOutputSink` (device-less sink running the production callback), `TestAudioOutput` and `OutputControl::test_audio_output()` PCM probes. Callback now counts one underrun per render call instead of per scratch block. Tests: `tests/playback_output.rs`, `playback::ring_tests`.
+- Orthic-Labs/rightkit#454: `audio_sync::align_pcm(camera, mic, max_offset_ms) -> PcmAlignment` (highest-energy camera reference, 16 kHz, 0.30 NCC floor), re-exported with `SAMPLE_RATE`. Failures are `AudioError::Invalid` with a `no mic alignment` message (no new `AudioError` variant). `mic_align` and `room_fill` were already on main in 0.3.1.
+- Orthic-Labs/rightkit#740: `wav::read_wav_mono_f32_prefix(path, max_seconds)` and `wav::read_wav_16k_mono_prefix(path, max_seconds)` decode only the first `max_seconds` of the data chunk; shorter files return everything, negative or non-finite durations return `Invalid`.
+
 ## 0.3.1 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Orthic-Labs/rightkit#454: new `mic_align` (`align_mic`, `AlignParams`, `MicAlignment`): mic-to-camera lag by mean-removed normalized cross-correlation, coarse 4x-decimated full-range pass then a full-rate fine pass, with confidence and peak margin. New `room_fill` (`room_tone_fill`, `room_tone_bed`, `FillParams`, `ToneFill`, `rms`, `encode_mono_f32_wav`): looped room-tone fill with equal-power crossfaded seams, scaled to the measured RMS plus `gain_db`. Lifted from CutRight `cutright-audio`, with its tests. Not compiled or run.
