+
+## Thread-owned app playback (G3)
+
+`OutputSession::start(source, PlaybackOptions)` returns Send-safe `OutputPlayback`; cpal
+stream & decoder stay on one owner thread. Implement `PlaybackSource` for decoded,
+random-access interleaved PCM. Decoder returns exactly requested frame count. Source rate,
+channel count & total frames stay fixed for session lifetime. `decode_range` may allocate
+or block; it never runs in callback. Drop waits for current decode before joining owner.
+
+```rust,no_run
+use rightkit_audio::playback::{OutputSession, PlaybackOptions, PlaybackSource};
+# fn preview(source: impl PlaybackSource) -> Result<(), rightkit_audio::AudioError> {
+let audio = OutputSession::start(source, PlaybackOptions::default())?;
+audio.set_gain(0.0)?; // preview mute; export PCM remains untouched
+audio.seek_samples(48_000); // absolute source frame at source sample rate
+audio.set_speed(1.5)?;
+audio.resume();
+let source_frame = audio.cursor_samples();
+let device_format = audio.output().format();
+let underruns = audio.output().stats().underruns;
+audio.stop(); // keeps queue & device; resume continues
+audio.flush();
+# let _ = (source_frame, device_format, underruns);
+# Ok(())
+# }
+```
+
+Device defaults negotiate actual rate, channels & sample representation. Feeder converts
+source PCM to device layout with linear interpolation, matching preview varispeed
+(pitch follows speed). Mono is duplicated; extra output channels repeat final source
+channel; fewer output channels select corresponding source channels. This matches
+CutRight's stereo channel selection, including mono selecting left. Source & output rings
+remain bounded. Underrun produces silence & stalls source clock; pause also holds clock.
+Seek & speed changes discard buffered audio through flush generations. Already submitted
+hardware audio remains subject to device latency. Call transport methods on `OutputPlayback`;
+use `output()` for gain, mute, format, stats & PCM probes.
+
+For silent QA from first sample, pass `PlaybackOptions { gain: OutputGain::new(0.0)?, ..Default::default() }`.
+Gain is initialized before callback creation. Clone `OutputGain` across reopens to retain app volume preference. Later gain/mute changes ramp within callback;
+probe peaks are cumulative, including ramps. Feature `test-mode` exposes
+`audio.output().test_audio_output()` with `samples: u64`, `pre_gain_peak_abs: f64` &
+`peak_abs: f64`. No probes, fake sink or environment overrides exist without feature.
+
+Device-less tests: `rustright cargo test -p rightkit-audio --no-default-features --features playback,test-mode --lib --test playback_output`.
+G3 has not been built or run: scratch compilation was refused by RustRight with
+`RK_NOT_PRIMARY_CHECKOUT`. Rustfmt syntax/format checks & patch applicability are recorded
+in G3 delivery notes.
